# Procedural Sprite Manager (Sanitized Backup)

This backup outlines the procedural sprite manager at a summary level suitable for external sharing.

## Lifecycle
- Initialization wires the renderer dependencies and prepares shared registries.
- Shutdown releases renderer references and clears active instances.
- Detailed validation paths, error metrics, and recovery routines are [REDACTED].

## Registration
- Gameplay systems register and deregister sprite instances so the manager can coordinate updates and drawing.
- Registry schemas, identifier formats, and automated reconciliation steps are [REDACTED].

## Rendering
- Draw sweeps iterate live instances, configure the appropriate render pass, and submit procedural geometry.
- Batching rules, warning thresholds, and pass-transition safeguards are [REDACTED].

## Limitations
- Current constraints include minimal built-in transform data and limited culling support.
- Backlog priorities, optimization roadmaps, and profiling data are [REDACTED].
